            <ArticleTitle>Uterus duplex with a unilaterally imperforate vagina--diagnosis and treatment. Report of two cases and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>247-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Severe cyclic dysmenorrhoea in a young woman with a unilateral abdominopelvic mass terminating in a purpuric bulge in the lateral vaginal wall, and resulting in renal agenesis ipsilateral to the pelvic mass, suggests uterus didelphys with unilaterally imperforate vagina. A report of two cases, their diagnostic and therapeutic approach and review of the literature are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
